#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
#
# btrfs-stall-report
#
# Installed by btrfs-setup.sh (CST). Summarises what
# btrfs-stall-monitord (and, if installed, below) recorded for a time window:
# was storage the bottleneck, and if so why. No root needed.
#
#   btrfs-stall-report                        last 30 minutes
#   btrfs-stall-report --since '20 min ago'   (anything `date -d` accepts, or @epoch)
#   btrfs-stall-report --since 10:30 --until 10:45 -v
#   btrfs-stall-report --since '1 day ago' --json
#
# Run the workload normally (cargo test, docker compose up, ...); query the
# window afterwards. Nothing has to wrap the command. Data reaches disk about
# every 10 s, so query ~15 s after the slow part ends.

